# Pig Animations (single GLB)

All pig clips live in **`public/models/pig/pig.glb`**. Registry: `PIG_MODEL` + `PIG_CLIPS` in `src/constants/models.ts`.

The GLB Armature is **cm-scaled (0.01)**. `fitSkinnedToHeight` must call `updateMatrixWorld(true)` and use `PIG_TARGET_HEIGHT` (~1.65m). Do not set height to a few centimeters as a workaround.

## Clip names (inside pig.glb)

GLTFLoader names (use these). Ignore `Armature|*|baselayer` (bind/T-pose) and `*.001` duplicates.

| Key | Clip name | Loop |
|-----|-----------|------|
| walk / walkGun | Walking | yes |
| run | Running | yes |
| aim / shoot | Walking (paused) | yes |
| deathAbdominal / deathShot | Dead | no |

There is **no idle / aim / shoot clip** in the current file. Aim and shoot freeze a walk pose (`speed={0}`).

## In-place clips + world locomotion

`Walking` / `Running` do **not** travel (hips sway in place). Pigs move because `update-soldiers.ts` writes `soldier.position` each frame.

- Patrol (`biped`): keep `PIG_WALK_SPEED`, face **velocity** (`atan2(vx, vz)` — Mixamo +Z forward).
- Flee: `PIG_RUN_SPEED`, face velocity, drop weapon.
- Aim / shoot: velocity 0, face the drone, pause walk clip. Aim only during a short windup (`cool <= 35`); otherwise patrol.
- Never multiply velocity by `0.1` (that leftover made them treadmill in place).

## Component pattern

- Use `PigAnimatedModel` — one `useGLTF` load, `SkeletonUtils.clone`, `useAnimations(animations, cloneRef)` on the **cloned mesh ref**.
- Crossfade with `fadeIn` / `fadeOut` when switching clips; do **not** remount the model per state.
- AK weapon is a separate `WeaponAk` attach — hidden during aim/shoot/run and when `weaponDropped`.

## Behavior → animation

| `Soldier.behavior` | Clip | Notes |
|--------------------|------|-------|
| biped | walkGun | patrol, actually translates |
| aim | Walking paused | drone in range, on cooldown |
| shoot | Walking paused | fires bullet, `shootTimer` counts down |
| flee | run | cowardly pigs or incoming munition; drops weapon |
| dead | Dead | ram and munition both use `deathShot` (same explosion death) |

## FPV ram (drone contact)

Touching a pig is a kamikaze blast: same death as a rugby explosion **plus** `checkExplosion` at the impact.

- 3D contact only (`dist3 < RAM_RADIUS`, ~1.85). Do not use a large XZ flyover radius.
- Death variant is `shot` (same clip/splat as munitions). Then run `checkExplosion` with `forceBig` so fire, smoke, and pig splat spawn.
- Splash can kill nearby pigs / reds / drones in the blast. Direct ram still costs the drone `RAM_DAMAGE`.
- `MIN_ALTITUDE` stays low enough (~0.5) that the drone can dive into torso height.

## AI (update-soldiers.ts)

- `cowardly` pigs (~45%) flee when drone within 14m and spot range 22m.
- Non-cowardly pigs aim/shoot instead of fleeing.
- Fleeing always sets `weaponDropped = true`.
